HELIX-XML

lib/helix-xml/ is a permanent MIT-licensed fork of the declarative XML UI engine
that shipped inside LVGL core until v9.5 removed it. It was taken from LVGL at
commit a15dcbeb5 (v9.4.0-358, 2026-01-26), the last commit before the removal,
at which point LVGL's LICENCE.txt was plain MIT and no separate license covered
the XML sources.

Unlike the rest of this repository, HelixScreen's own contributions inside
lib/helix-xml/ are licensed MIT rather than GPL-3.0-or-later, so that the engine
remains usable and redistributable as a standalone MIT library. Per-file SPDX
headers record whether each file is unmodified LVGL code, LVGL code modified by
356C LLC, or written for helix-xml.

See lib/helix-xml/LICENSE, lib/helix-xml/README.md, and
docs/devel/LVGL_XML_SITUATION.md.

